     <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>OBAT OIL</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise Nearly 3% as Trump Threatens Iran Backers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    As of 11:30 a.m. WAT, Brent crude was trading at $93.82 per barrel, up $2.20 or 2.40% , while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $86.65 per barrel. The latest advance came after U.S. President Donald Trump announced what he described as the “most crushing economic operation” against Iran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-nearly-3-as-trump-threatens-iran-backers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    BREAKING: Dangote Refinery Raises Diesel Price by ₦100 to ₦1,670/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery has increased its Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) price by ₦100 per litre. The increase comes amid a rise in international crude oil prices, with Brent crude recently trading above $93 per barrel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/breaking-dangote-refinery-raises-diesel-price-by-100-to-1670litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Atiku Pledges to Restore Fuel Subsidy if Elected in 2027\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has pledged to reinstate Nigeria’s fuel subsidy if he wins the presidency in the 2027 general election. Atiku, who is the presidential candidate of the African Democratic Congress (ADC), said he initially did not oppose the decision to remove the subsidy. The decision led to a sharp increase in petrol prices and contributed to higher transportation costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/atiku-pledges-to-restore-fuel-subsidy-if-elected-in-2027\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Regulatory Uncertainty Could Drive Investors Away From Nigeria’s Oil Sector – Osifo\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    PENGASSAN President, Comrade Festus Osifo, called for a predictable, transparent and efficient regulatory system. He said the Petroleum Industry Act, PIA, 2021, was a major milestone in the country’s long-running effort to reform the sector.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/regulatory-uncertainty-could-drive-investors-away-from-nigerias-oil-sector-osifo\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Subsidy, ₦200/Litre Petrol Price Would Have Crushed Dangote Refinery — FG\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has said that the Dangote Petroleum Refinery could not have operated commercially under Nigeria’s former petrol subsidy regime. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, stated this in Abuja. He said the removal of the petrol subsidy, alongside the unification of the foreign exchange market, came with significant costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/subsidy-200litre-petrol-price-would-have-crushed-dangote-refinery-fg\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
